+# chore(housekeeping): close 19 stale auto-filed CI orders polluting the runway queue
+
+## Problem
+The runway queue carries 19 CI-failure orders that are already resolved; they keep
+`status:runway` visible and drown real work. Verified stale as of 2026-10-27:
+
+- 8x "Open Unified Pipeline failed on 1426/merge" (#1427-#1434): PR #1426 is
+  CLOSED (0 open PRs on the repo), and open main is GREEN (run 40467936110).
+- 8x core/studio main failures (#1401,#1402,#1404,#1408,#1412,#1414,#1416 + the
+  studio 40397847487/#1425): both mains are GREEN with fixes landed — core run
+  40396646408 success (carries the core/__init__ lazy-export fix), studio run
+  40411503150 success (carries the AdminShell/AdminConsole fixes). The only
+  remaining core failure (#1445, nightly PyErrorFix job) is tracked separately
+  by #1446 with a fix PR open.
+- #1417/#1418 (claimed CI orders): fixes landed via the sync bot; leases can be
+  released and orders closed as done.
+
+## Requested action
+Close the listed orders as "stale — superseded by green mains" (or let the
+federated CI watcher auto-close on green); release the two claimed leases.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- [ ] Runway queue contains no order older than the latest green run on its repo
+- [ ] #1417/#1418 leases released
+- [ ] #1445/#1446 remain the only live CI items (until PyErrorFix lands)
+
+## Reflection Evidence
+**Why:** A runway queue that mostly contains resolved failures misroutes coder
+agents and hides the real P0; hygiene here has outsized routing value for every
+future bridge task.
+**Alternatives rejected:**
+- Leave auto-closure to the watcher: it demonstrably has not closed them across
+  two green cycles; explicit close avoids weeks of noise.
+- Batch-close via a bot without evidence: each close above carries its
+  superseding green run id for auditability.
